not visited, then return here. The same lamp will be waiting; your recorded route will be different.", "sha256": "9013e3e18fb9145f995acb59b8c97912e33c44e2935c4f5681e8087493b24ddf", "retained": true}, "RX3@6fb19fb9535d": {"page_id": "RX3", "text": "A small lamp shines beside the garden gate.\n\nSynthetic demonstration — The garden.\n\nThe window is still visible behind you. In an ordinary journey you could return now. In the recurrence demonstration, visit one more new room first.", "sha256": "6fb19fb9535d8025d99c13860c92a5f967c7ec3e83c796b8346e39e101e9ca71", "retained": true}, "RX5@70c726eb9ba5": {"page_id": "RX5", "text": "A lamp is reflected in the water.\n\nSynthetic demonstration — The pool.\n\nYou can see the starting window in the reflection. After two outward arrivals, the return to that exact room becomes available.", "sha256": "70c726eb9ba5fc7cd85ba0e452e5a33e28dbd6008635ef78b1a11e7c27c2aa9e", "retained": true}, "RX7@cb01ce8b6def": {"page_id": "RX7", "text": "A shaded lamp lights a narrow stair.\n\nSynthetic demonstration — The stair.\n\nThis is another outward choice. A room already visited cannot count as a new room; the journey remembers each arrival in order.", "sha256": "cb01ce8b6def4ba44f57f39a11b6e38270edda66d9da93b1348ec5a15c0286ee", "retained": true}}}
